    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee is refunded in full. The fee charged was SGD 4.50 (EV-FARE-02723: cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). Under POL-NS-01 a no-show fee is chargeable only if all four limbs hold. Limb (d) fails: the trip was terminated by the driver with cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE (EV-TRIP-02723), which is not one of the three codes the limb recognises and which the clause treats as the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider. Because the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius (EV-GPS-02723: one in-geofence run, 380 s, 39 qualifying fixes), POL-NS-01 directs a full refund of the cancellation fee with no driver compensation, plus the driver-education referral above. Independently, POL-NS-04 exonerates the rider: she sent a locating message during the waiting window ('at the lift lobby', 12:00:59, EV-CHAT-02723); the driver neither replied within 120 s nor made an in-app call before cancelling at 12:06:23 (EV-TRIP-02723, in_app_calls empty); and her device sat inside the 100 m rider-presence radius for all 67 of her qualifying fixes (mean 11.7 m, max 15.5 m). The refund is FULL_REFUND of the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line. Surviving claims, answered together where they make the same point: (1) The driver's dwell point is right on the facts — the in-geofence dwell was 380 s against the 180 s free waiting period in force — and the arrival marker was not false (first in-geofence fix 11:59:59 matches the 'arrived' event, no motion at the marker), so POL-NS-05 does not move the clock. But a sufficient dwell and a true marker cannot rescue a fee whose limb (d) fails. (2) The rider's POL-NS-06 shortfall argument is rejected: 380 s exceeds the 180 s free waiting period POL-NS-01(c) requires, and the 300 s figure in fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec is a version-1 interpretive field that the resolution rule says is never applied to a record carrying platform_policy — and 380 s exceeds it in any event. (3) The driver's POL-NS-03 point is accepted: the stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius, so the wrong-entrance route is closed. (4) Driver compensation of SGD 3.60 (80 percent of 4.50, EV-FARE-02723) is not payable: POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 satisfied in full, and it is not; and NO_ACTION — leaving the charge in place — is not open where limb (d) fails. (5) The anti-farming check is not tripped (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 0 against 114 completed trips in 30 days; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d 0), and neither POL-NS-09(c) nor (d) is engaged, so there is no abuse escalation. (6) EV-ADVIS-02723-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT); it decides nothing here, because with a single in-geofence interval and a 380 s dwell there is no shortfall for POL-NS-06(i) to cure, and under POL-NS-11/NS-08 it does not impair the driver's trace or cap confidence. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d): no clock skew (arrival event 11:59:59 = first fix 11:59:59), no trace gap (100% coverage, 75 fixes, max gap 0 s), the chat carries the 2 messages the trip record counts, and the fare line reconciles to platform_policy at SGD 4.50 — so no escalation under POL-NS-09. Confidence is 0.95: the deciding facts rest on artifacts at weight 1.0. The monetary effect is SGD 4.50, at or below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes automatically."
