{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-01: cancellation reason code mis-selection by driver DRV-09723 — trip TRP-02723 was terminated under DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE although the driver's stationary fixes lay inside the POL-NS-02 arrival radius; refer as a driver-education item on the correct no-show codes (RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE, EXCESSIVE_WAIT)."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged to the rider is refunded in full (amount_sgd 4.50), and no driver compensation is payable (driver_compensation_sgd null). This is a provisional ruling made without human review. Either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04, and the monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so the refund executes automatically.\n\nWhat happened is not seriously disputed. DRV-09723 was assigned at 11:54:58, tapped 'I'm Here' at 11:59:59, and the GPS trace EV-GPS-02723 places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 11:59:59 to 12:06:19 — a continuous 380-second in-geofence run of 39 qualifying fixes, no gaps, 100% coverage. The rider's own track in the same trace sits within 15.5 m of the pin for the whole window. In chat (EV-CHAT-02723) the driver asked 'cannot find you, where are you' at 12:00:29 and the rider answered 'at the lift lobby' at 12:00:59.\n\nTwo independent routes make the fee unchargeable.\n\nFirst, POL-NS-01 limb (d). The anchor clause requires the trip to be terminated under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. The trip record EV-TRIP-02723 shows cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which POL-NS-01(d) itself names as the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider and which does not satisfy limb (d). The driver's advocate conceded exactly this, and the driver's own counterparty statement says the same. POL-NS-01's own text then fixes the outcome for this configuration: where the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, the fee is not chargeable, the ruling is FULL_REFUND of the cancellation fee with no driver compensation, and the mis-selected reason code is referred as a driver-education item. That is this case — the fixes are inside the radius, not outside it, so POL-NS-03 does not apply.\n\nSecond, POL-NS-04. (a) The rider sent a locating message inside the waiting window ('at the lift lobby' — an entrance identifier). (b) The driver neither replied in chat within 120 seconds of that message nor placed an in-app call before cancelling (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty). (c) The rider's own track puts her within the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius on every qualifying fix. All three limbs hold, so the rider is exonerated and the fee is refunded in full with no driver compensation.\n\nThe driver's surviving arguments are answered. The 380-second dwell does exceed the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, the figure read from the record itself), and the arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 — the 11:59:59 marker matches the first qualifying in-geofence fix and the driver was stationary at it — but neither fact makes the fee chargeable, because limb (d) is the rider-fault limb and the driver's own reason code defeats it. EV-FARE-02723 shows the fee line of SGD 4.50 reconciles with platform_policy, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect, but that only confirms the amount, not its chargeability; the computed driver compensation of SGD 3.60 is not payable because POL-NS-07 pays only on a fee that survives POL-NS-01. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 0 against 114 completed trips in 30 days), so compensation is not withheld on that ground — it simply never arises. The NO_ACTION argument is rejected: POL-GEN-03 makes NO_ACTION party-relative on a rider-filed dispute, and it cannot be used to convert a failed limb (d) into a driver payout.\n\nThe rider's advocate's POL-NS-06 submission is rejected on the merits: the required minimum dwell for this record is the 180-second free waiting period the record carries, not the 300-second version-1 figure, which fee_schedule says is never applied to a record carrying platform_policy; 380 seconds exceeds 180 seconds, so there is no shortfall and no refund route is needed under POL-NS-06.\n\nNo escalation applies. Confidence is above the POL-NS-09 floor of 0.70; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; neither party's repeat-dispute counters reach POL-NS-09(c) or (d); and no deciding fact rests on an impaired artifact. The only artifact below full weight is the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02723-01, which is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); nobody needs it, because the driver held one continuous 380-second run and never required accumulated dwell, so it carries no deciding fact and does not cap confidence under POL-GEN-02(2). All artifacts that do carry the deciding facts (EV-TRIP-02723, EV-GPS-02723, EV-CHAT-02723) stand at weight 1.0, so the cap is 1.0.\n\nOne submission was discarded at the citation check: the driver's claim resting on the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02723-01 failed to disclose that artifact's impairment and issue code, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires."
  },
